        "eventMetadata": {
          "context_description": "Xi Jinping\u2019s consolidated dominance within the Chinese Communist Party and military underpins trader consensus against his removal before 2027. Ongoing purges of senior officials, including multiple Politburo and Central Military Commission members through mid-2026, have reinforced loyalty networks and eliminated visible rivals without signs of elite fragmentation. No successor has been elevated ahead of the expected 21st Party Congress later in 2027, and institutional norms around age limits appear suspended for the general secretary and CMC chairman roles. Recent leadership meetings and personnel projections indicate continuity rather than transition. While a sudden health event, unanticipated internal realignment, or major policy reversal could still shift dynamics, available evidence shows no erosion of his authority in the near term.",
          "context_requires_regen": true,
